__ci'a__ was once the official modal for ''ciska'', but it was considered ((malglico)), since the concept actually required was one of authorship rather than scribehood. It was replaced by ((fi'e)), derived from ((finti)).  Since then it has remained an ((unassigned cmavo)).

See:

* [http://wiw.org/~jkominek/lojban/9104/msg00082.html] for a representative rant against ''ci'a'' by ((Nick Nicholas)),
* [http://wiw.org/~jkominek/lojban/9106/msg00007.html] for a response by ((Bob LeChevalier)),
* [http://wiw.org/~jkominek/lojban/9106/msg00043.html] for the grammar change that made ''fi'e'' available,
* [http://wiw.org/~jkominek/lojban/9106/msg00045.html] for the proposal to differentiate ''ci'a'' and ''fi'e'' modal,
* [http://wiw.org/~jkominek/lojban/9201/msg00074.html] as proof of the early effacement of the cmavo.
